theorem a-part-with-a-size
  note        A letter running over the parts of X is a set, so |W| is its
              size, and a message says the claim back as the page writes it.
  let X be a set                                                      (H1)
  assume there is W ⊆ X with 1 ≤ |W|                                  (H2)
  then there is W ⊆ X with 1 ≤ |W|

1.  There is W ⊆ X with 1 ≤ |W|.
    restate H2

theorem every-part-with-a-size
  note        The same of a letter every part of X fills.
  let X be a set                                                      (H1)
  assume for all W ⊆ X, |W| ≤ 2                                       (H2)
  then for all W ⊆ X, |W| ≤ 2

1.  For all W ⊆ X, |W| ≤ 2.
    restate H2
